In article <JuTsaB1w164w@cellar.org>, hacksaw@cellar.org (Hacksaw) writes...
>   A local UNIX system recently installed NetHack(on older version, I think) 

     Get the most recent version (3.0j aka 3.0pl10 and 3.0.10) so that you
don't have to rediscover all the old bugs that have already been fixed.
The 'v' command will show you the version you've got, and '#version' will
show what options it was built with.

> Everytime I play, level one works fine... except for trying to goto 
>level 2. I get a "A mysterious force prevents you from going down" message. 

     When you change levels, the level that you're leaving is written into
a file so that memory can be re-used for the one you're going to.  The
message is telling you that NetHack is unable to save the old level.  Most
likely reason is that the directory permissions don't allow you to write
files there.  You should also test the 'S' command to see whether it will
let you save games.  Save files are written to a subdirectory, so there
are two places where you need to be able to write files.

